course: dictionary
lesson: 9106
title: Smartly: neat, quick or clever
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Smartly is an adverb. It tells you how something is done, and it can have more than one meaning. The words around it are its context, and they show you which meaning fits. «Pupils were asked to dress smartly for the school photo» is about clothes: smartly means in a neat, tidy and good-looking way.
explain: «He rapped smartly on the door» is about movement. Rapped is a fast, sharp knock, so smartly means quickly and firmly. Try the meaning in the sentence: «He rapped neatly on the door» sounds odd, but «He rapped quickly and firmly on the door» makes sense.
explain: Smartly can also mean cleverly. In the Wind in the Willows, animals often step or reply smartly. When you meet smartly, ask what is happening: is it about clothes, movement or thinking? The clue will tell you which meaning to use.
fact: Smartly is an adverb, so it often comes after a verb, as in «stepped smartly».
fact: «Smartly» means in a neat, tidy and good-looking way, especially about clothes, as in «dressed smartly».
fact: «Smartly» means quickly and sharply, as in «rapped smartly on the door»: a quick, firm knock.
fact: «Smartly» can mean cleverly.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «He rapped smartly on the door.» What does smartly mean here? | *Quickly and firmly | Slowly and sadly | Quietly, so no one heard | Wearing neat clothes
exercise: Pupils are asked to dress smartly for the concert. What does smartly mean? | Loudly and proudly | Messy and muddy | *Neat, tidy and good-looking | Quickly and sharply
exercise: «The soldier turned smartly and marched away.» Find and copy the word that tells how he turned. | away | *smartly | soldier | marched
test: «Kid gloves were part of being smartly dressed.» What does smartly mean in this sentence? | Quick and sharp | Dirty and torn | Cleverly | *Neat and good-looking, especially in clothes
test: «The Rabbit stepped smartly forward.» What does smartly suggest? | Sleepy, slow movement | Loud singing | Dirty clothes | *Quick, brisk movement
exam: «The fox gave a smartly worded reply that fooled everyone.» What does smartly mean here? | Slowly | Dirty | *Cleverly | Loudly
